  "body": "Currently, the [`HIDDevice.forget()` method steps](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#dom-hiddevice-forget) do not specify how to handle calls made when the relevant global object's associated `Document` is not [fully active](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#fully-active) (for example, when the frame is in pending deletion / running `unload` handlers after navigating away).\n\nRevoking device permissions from a document that is no longer fully active should not be allowed, and silently resolving the promise misleads callers into believing the permission revocation succeeded.\n\n`HIDDevice.forget()` should check if the document is fully active and, if not, reject the promise with an `\"InvalidStateError\"` `DOMException`.\n\n[Chromium CL for context](https://crrev.com/c/8499468)",
